  </metadata>
  <prompt>Add a `workspace.active_widget_changed` subscriber to ConversationPane that stores `{ widgetType, contextType, tabId, displayName, compactState }` in a ref, plus a seam test.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React/TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 frontend expertise; comfortable extending PaneEventBus subscriptions and writing seam tests without re-render churn.</role>
  <goal>Switching the active Workspace tab updates the focus ref; a seam test verifies the subscriber.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-A1 — the Assistant has no active-tab tracking today. `active_widget_changed` is broadcast by WorkspacePane.tsx:586 and consumed only by ReviewCompleteToast; ConversationPane's usePaneEvent('workspace') subscription (:2362) handles only widget_load, with no active-tab branch.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/events/PaneEventTypes.ts (read the active_widget_changed payload)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-030">Use the existing PaneEventBus `usePaneEvent('workspace', …)` subscription pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Store in a ref (not state) to avoid re-render churn.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKEAI-WORKSPACE-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-030-pane-event-bus.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read PaneEventTypes active_widget_changed payload (widgetType, widgetData, tabId, displayName).</step>
    <step order="2">Add a usePaneEvent('workspace') handler branch for active_widget_changed that writes the focus ref.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a seam test asserting the ref updates on an active_widget_changed event.</step>
    <step order="4">Build + test.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If active_widget_changed is not actually broadcast for the email widget path, STOP and escalate rather than inventing a new event.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Focus ref updates">
      <steps>Switch the active tab; verify (via the dev trace or a temporary log) the focus ref reflects the new tab. Include an ADR-021 dark-mode no-regression check.</steps>
      <expected>Focus ref reflects the newly-active tab; no dark-mode regressions.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <justification>
    <existing>ConversationPane usePaneEvent('workspace') at :2362 handles only widget_load — no active-tab branch.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend the existing workspace subscription with an active_widget_changed branch.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>'summarize this' keeps resolving against the server UpdatedAt heuristic, not the focused tab.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">the seam test file</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Switching the active tab updates the focus ref.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seam test passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No SprkChat fork.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Ref shape must match FR-A1 exactly: { widgetType, contextType, tabId, displayName, compactState }.</notes>
